              {
                "text": "**Analyzing Path Formation**\n\nI'm working on path generation using color 3 (green). In training example 1, I've identified the starting and stopping points for these paths. Row 2 extends from column 0 to 4 with the color 3. A color 6 block is at (2,5), so the path can't continue. I've also identified a vertical run from (3,4) to (5,4).\n\n\n**Investigating Turning Logic**\n\nI'm now focusing on the turning behavior of the paths. I've been analyzing how paths generated with color 3 (green) react to different blockers, specifically 6 and 8. In Train 1, 6 makes it go down, in Train 3, 8 makes it go up, and in Train 4, the presence of 6 makes the path turn down, while 8 seems to be irrelevant if another blocker exists on the same row. I'm hypothesizing the path direction (up or down) depends on the value of the blocker.\n\n\n",
                "type": "reasoning_text"
              }
            ],
            "encrypted_content": null,
