              {
                "annotations": [],
                "text": "An analysis of the training examples reveals the following rule:\n\n1. A ray of green (`3`) starts at the position of the original `3` (at column 0) and travels to the right along its row.\n2. If it encounters magenta (`6`) in its row, it stops in the column immediately before `6` and turns **DOWN**, continuing in that column all the way to the bottom edge of the grid.\n3. If it encounters teal (`8`) in its row, it stops in the column immediately before `8` and turns **UP**, continuing in that column all the way to the top edge of the grid.\n4. If neither obstacle is in its row, it continues straight to the right edge of the grid.\n5. All other colored cells remain unchanged.\n\nPlease provide the test input grid.",
